<section class="home-intro">
	<h1 class="home-title">Hi, I’m Chi!</h1>
	<p>
		I’m a software engineer on the Lakebase team at Databricks. Before that, I studied computer science at Shanghai Jiao Tong University and Carnegie Mellon University.
	</p>
	<p>
		I work on database systems and enjoy explaining how they work. I helped build <a href="https://github.com/cmu-db/bustub">BusTub</a>, the educational database used in CMU’s database course. I also created two courses: <a href="https://github.com/skyzh/mini-lsm">mini-lsm</a>, where you build a storage engine from scratch, and <a href="https://github.com/skyzh/tiny-llm">tiny-llm</a>, where you build an LLM inference engine.
	</p>
	<p>
		Over the years, I’ve found that I most enjoy solving hard problems in real systems and making them reliable for the people who depend on them. I hope to continue this work and share what I learn along the way.
	</p>
	<div class="fun-facts">
		<h2>Fun facts about me</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>I go by Chi when there’s no other Chi in the room; otherwise, Alex. Chi is pronounced “chee.”</li>
			<li>I speak Mandarin, English, and Shanghainese, plus a little Japanese.</li>
			<li>I started programming at nine. Rust became my favorite language in 2018, and TiKV got me into databases in 2020.</li>
			<li>I helped make CMU’s <a href="https://15445.courses.cs.cmu.edu/">15-445</a> projects more engaging. In Fall 2023, I might accidentally have made them ridiculously hard.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

